{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# End-to-end RAG API lab\n","\n","This notebook turns retrieval-augmented generation into a backend workflow: ingest -> index -> retrieve -> generate -> cite -> measure."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from dataclasses import dataclass\n","\n","@dataclass(frozen=True)\n","class Chunk:\n","    id: str\n","    text: str\n","    source: str\n","    document_version: str\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["documents = [\n","    Chunk('c1', 'FastAPI uses Pydantic models for request validation.', 'fastapi.md', 'v1'),\n","    Chunk('c2', 'Redis is useful for caching and rate limiting.', 'redis.md', 'v3'),\n"]\n","\n","def retrieve(query: str, chunks: list[Chunk], top_k: int = 2) -> list[Chunk]:\n","    # Replace this lexical baseline with embeddings/vector search.\n","    terms = set(query.lower().split())\n","    scored = [(len(terms & set(c.text.lower().split())), c) for c in chunks]\n","    return [c for score, c in sorted(scored, key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True) if score > 0][:top_k]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["question = 'How does FastAPI validate requests?'\n","hits = retrieve(question, documents)\n","context = '\\n\\n'.join(f'[{c.id}] {c.text}' for c in hits)\n","print(context)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Backend implementation exercises\n","\n","1. Create `/v1/answers` in FastAPI.\n","2. Add authentication and tenant isolation.\n","3. Replace lexical search with an embedding store.\n","4. Add document ingestion as a background job.\n","5. Return source IDs/citations with the answer.\n","6. Enforce a context/token budget.\n","7. Add model timeout and fallback behavior.\n","8. Track retrieval latency, generation latency, token usage, and estimated cost.\n","9. Build a golden evaluation set and score retrieval separately from generation.\n","10. Test deleted documents, stale versions, empty retrieval, provider failure, and prompt injection."]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}